{{!
    @template tool_vae/fiche_cell

    A cell of the table of the preview of an import of records: the number of a record in bold and its title under it, or
    the blocs of the export folded away, then lines one under the other, each a div with or without a class. The parts touch,
    with nothing between them: the line breaks of this template are carried by comments.

    Every text comes from the context, given by tool_vae\output\fiche_cell. The template holds no logic. The texts are
    escaped (double braces). One key is HTML (triple braces): texthtml, the sentence of a refusal, made safe by
    tool_vae\local\fiche_messages::html() (its parameters are escaped there).

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * record - false, or an object {number, title}: the header of the row; title is false or an object {label}
    * blocs - false, or an object {summary, rows}: the blocs of the export; rows is an array of objects {rang, label}
    * lines - array of objects {classed, text, html}: classed is false or an object {name}; text is false or an object
      {label}; html is false or an object {texthtml}

    Example context (json):
    {
        "record": {"number": "RNCP99001", "title": {"label": "Diplôme inventé"} },
        "blocs": {"summary": "2 blocs", "rows": [{"rang": "BC01", "label": "Premier bloc"}]},
        "lines": [
            {"classed": {"name": "small"}, "text": {"label": "Active"}, "html": false},
            {"classed": false, "text": false, "html": {"texthtml": "The number is not in the export."} }
        ]
    }
}}
{{#record}}<strong>{{number}}</strong>{{#title}}<div>{{label}}</div>{{/title}}{{/record}}{{!
}}{{#blocs}}<details><summary>{{summary}}</summary><ul>{{!
}}{{#rows}}<li><strong>{{rang}}</strong> {{label}}</li>{{/rows}}</ul></details>{{/blocs}}{{!
}}{{#lines}}<div{{#classed}} class="{{name}}"{{/classed}}>{{!
}}{{#text}}{{label}}{{/text}}{{#html}}{{{texthtml}}}{{/html}}</div>{{/lines}}
